# Vault writing

Full tag audit workflow: `.cursor/skills/vault-tags/` (see `taxonomy.md`).

## Wikilinks

- Link a concept **once per page**, on the first useful mention; later repeats stay plain text.
- If two display words share one note (Blackstone / Illumination), link only one in that sentence.
- **Exceptions**: Quick links, hubs, Bases — intentional link lists are fine.

## Aliases

- Use `aliases` for search names and short forms people will type or link (`Stonewake`, `Bright Mother`, `the Mundane`).
- Prefer aliases over duplicate notes for alternate titles.
- Verb/forms that resolve to the same concept go on that note (`Illuminates`, `Illuminated` on Divine Illumination).
- Do not put aliases that belong on another note; do not use aliases as a second tagging system.

## Properties

Only these frontmatter keys:

| Key | Where | Notes |
|-----|--------|--------|
| `aliases` | any | YAML list |
| `tags` | any | kind tags only (below) |
| `publish` | any | unquoted `true` / `false` |
| `faction` | gods only | `Light` \| `Void` \| `Neutral` — **not** a tag |
| `title` | wiki home only | optional |

- Remove typos and unused keys. Never invent new properties without updating `taxonomy.md`.
- Bases filter gods with `faction:` + `God` tag — do not also tag Light/Void/Neutral.

## Tags

- Singular **Title Case**: `Place`, `Event`, `Concept`, `God`, `Faction`, `NPC`, `Player`, `Setting` (+ optional `Session`).
- One primary kind per note (folder default: Locations→Place, Events→Event, Lore→Concept / World Overview→Setting, Gods→God, Factions→Faction, PCs→Player).
- YAML list, one `- Tag` per line, sorted alphabetically. No plurals, no lowercase kinds (`place`), no subtypes like `city-state` unless we add them to taxonomy on purpose.
- `publish: true` for player-facing lore; `false` for Void gods, private PCs, DM-only stubs.

## Prose

- Short and concrete. No em dashes. Avoid AI filler.
- Placeholders stay obvious (`[[IDK YET WORLD]]`).

## Structure

- Combine notes only when terms are one system (Illumination + Blackstone). Otherwise one idea per note.
- Folders: `Locations/`, `Events/`, `Lore/`, `People/Gods/`, `Factions/`, `People/PCs/`.
